WEBVTT

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.960
What are you doing?

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.430
What do you mean, what? Playing piano.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.410
I can see that, but why?

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.350
You got a problem with it?

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.370
No, no problem. It's just unusual.

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.410
Even I play a little piano now and then.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.580
Sorry...

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.760
What?!

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.590
Jeez!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.930
Fu's easy to read.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.670
What's easy to read?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.670
Madoka, would you join us for a little training?

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.270
Sure.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.890
Jeez, I wonder what this is from?

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.060
Nice, Tatsuya.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.320
Time for a little break.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.130
How does it feel?

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.250
How does what feel?

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.060
Fu is your ex-girlfriend, right, Isamu?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.370
Yeah, but I don't really have any feelings about it.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.640
Fu has lots of crushes,

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.110
so I thought something like this would probably happen.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.330
I thought so.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.740
After all, you're short on those kind of feelings.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.750
Oh no, did I offend you?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.480
No, you're right. I am short on those feelings, aren't I?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.720
I'm sorry, that's not how I meant it.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.560
No, I'm not upset.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.120
Things like that... You don't realize unless somebody tells you.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.770
I see, so I'm short on those feelings.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.270
That's a bit of a discovery.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.200
Now, your status report on the Turangalila operational test.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:31.950
Before making it, I would like to ask why an individual from another company,

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.040
...uninvolved in this project, is at this table.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:44.530
We're having young Kazamatsuri join us as an observer in regards to issues of security, Dr. Enuma.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:51.400
You, too, are certainly aware that once the Turangalila becomes fully operational,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.460
...we must take even greater precautions.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:57.810
It's already been decided that security will be left to the military, correct?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:05.270
Gilgamesh can't possibly clear the outer walls and gain entry into the Turangalila.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.720
It seems my presence here is a nuisance.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.980
Kazamatsuri!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.230
So long as there's no consensus of opinions at the top, it's highly unlikely that I can be of any use.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:24.630
When the esteemed Dr. Enuma herself, who is in charge of this project, feels the need for our assistance,

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.070
...please call me again then.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.480
Once again, the report please, Dr. Enuma.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:45.320
The Turangalila is already ninety-nine percent completed.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:52.590
And we intend to carry out an operational test right on schedule, a week from now, on October 10th.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.470
You say you want the children's cooperation?

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.910
I want to show the executives that our security is flawless.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:16.750
I'm disinclined to use those children for such a purpose though.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:21.830
I myself want to confirm that there are no holes in our security,

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:24.390
...and it would be good training for them, wouldn't it?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.090
I suppose.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.060
Or perhaps, they've already had enough training at sneaking into places on their own accord.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.310
Very well.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.500
Thank you, Dr. Kageyama.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.370
May I ask one thing?

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.510
What might that be?

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:45.450
Why do you feel such antipathy towards Kazamatsuri?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.640
That man's a fiend!

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:54.050
The one who originally decided to use his company for our building's security was me.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.760
As I was proceeding with the October Project,

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.930
...Chairman Yuki introduced me to his private-sector military contracting subsidiary.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.500
It was that man's company.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:10.000
And then what they delivered were the Embryons.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.270
I was astonished at their capabilities.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:19.680
Without computer control, how could they acquire such detection and recognition capabilities?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:27.460
I was suspicious, so I thoroughly investigated their manufacturing process.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.890
That's when I discovered their true nature.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.900
Those things are the same as your children.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:39.730
What controls the Embryons is something grown from the ES cells of Orga.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.930
In other words, they're human.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:48.640
When I cornered him on this, that man answered very calmly...

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:55.350
You were doing even worse things at Heaven's Gate, weren't you, Dr. Enuma?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.850
You're the ones who made the world like this.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.690
There's nothing to say in response to that, is there?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.290
It's different though, the nature of the atrocity.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:19.470
What I'm doing now may not be any different from what he did either.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.880
That doesn't matter to you?

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.450
You're acting as a mother to them, right?

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.140
Thank you.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.510
I'd rather not do this kind of thing.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:55.850
Why?

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:59.780
Demolishing the gate and forcing our way in... We're not terrorists.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.290
What's the problem?

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.350
They told us we could use any method we want.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.290
Toru! Trade places!

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.630
Jeez...

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.400
You sound miserable.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.080
<i>Over there!</i>

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.100
<i>Wait!</i>

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:04.120
We'll hold them off. You two head for the next gate.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.080
Right!

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.270
Let's teleport inside.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:25.240
Right!

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.880
What's wrong?

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:32.970
Our Dynamis doesn't...

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.150
Isamu!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:38.920
What?

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.880
On the other side of the door...

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:51.950
What's there?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.100
<i>Mission complete. Mission complete.</i>

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:18.580
It's vexing, but I do need to put those robots to good use.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:24.320
So this means if this had been real, those children would have lost their lives.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.730
Here you go.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:51.860
Here's yours.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:53.020
Thank you.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:56.790
In the end, our job was just to get beaten, huh?

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.660
Oh, well, it just tells us that we can be used that way too.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.560
Right, it all depends on Little Hiroko's mood.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.340
It's really soon now, huh? That the sky is going to clear up?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.800
Maybe...

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.070
Who cares what color the sky is?

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.140
I'm going home.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.290
She's got it bad, huh?

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.560
Shouldn't she get that checked out by a doctor?

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:33.930
A doctor, huh?

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.600
To think the Orga children can't do a thing against them...

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:46.370
It means this is indeed tremendously effective.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.750
Is this...

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:53.480
It's fine. It's been through laundering.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:00.490
So this is Lapis Warka in its raw form.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.650
It's the first time I've seen the real thing.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.360
It's fresh from Uruk.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.840
For some reason the stone mined at Uruk, Ground Zero for XX,

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:18.110
...neutralizes Dynamis.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:24.340
Its very presence greatly suppresses the efficacy of that lot's Dynamis.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:30.310
This stone is also used in the equipment of your Blattaria Special Forces, as I recall.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:35.130
Yes, and in the outer walls of that Turangalila as well.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:40.400
That's why the members of Gilgamesh absolutely cannot teleport into it,

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.560
...and just by approaching it they're prey for our Embryons.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.570
It's nothing to smile about.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:50.270
Thanks to them, Dr. Enuma is trying harder and harder to displace you.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:56.510
That's fine with me. Strong-willed women are more satisfying to conquer.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.390
Fu!

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.260
Bingo.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.910
What the heck kind of dream was that?

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.300
I'm finished.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.810
What's wrong with that girl?

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.940
You know, the same thing as always.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.720
Oh...

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:16.160
Fu!

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.830
You say she's avoiding you?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.860
Yeah, I wonder if I did something to upset her?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.740
The story with Fu is that she likes you, Tatsuya.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:37.580
What?

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.950
You didn't notice?

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.290
There seems to be something about her physically.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.740
When she gets near the person she likes, she sneezes.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.910
It's probably a psychosomatic thing though.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:52.930
And right now, she's crazy about you, Tatsuya.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.670
This is kind of sudden, I don't know...

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.900
Why don't you try dating her?

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:59.340
But...

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:02.700
Try dating her, and if you don't like it, you can break up with her.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.200
I don't know if I can do that.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:10.810
As long as you don't mind the runny nose, Fu's a good woman.

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:16.320
Well, it's up to you.

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:19.260
But if you're not interested in dating her, you ought to tell it to her straight.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.920
She'll feel better that way too.

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:05.070
It's raining, huh?

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:06.300
Yeah...

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:12.640
Tomorrow's finally the day. I wonder if it'll stop?

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.080
Hope it clears up, huh?

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.270
Say...

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.640
What?

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:25.280
Nothing, you just seem to be in pretty rough shape.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.420
I'm short on Dynamis.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.330
Hey, give me some!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.450
Huh?

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:36.290
Madoka, your Dynamis... It feels good, you know.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:49.210
I got a nosebleed.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:50.440
Are you okay?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.390
I'm sorry!

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.960
Jerk! This kind of thing's just a friendly greeting, you know!

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.150
I'm going to sleep.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:37.680
This is the worst.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.830
Final power reactor check complete.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.970
Prepared to fill the vector potential regulator.

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:10.320
Preparation for anti-electron-neutrino irradiation complete!

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:17.520
Activate Turangalila.

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:32.940
What's happening?

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:21.420
What happened?

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:28.420
That's the blue sky?

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.800
It's creepy somehow, isn't it?

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:33.930
Yeah...

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:26.650
Well, well...

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:27.420
...ladies?

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.390
I believe at some point I'll have the opportunity to show them...

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.790
...and to your children.

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:33.990
Attacking in full force? That's convenient.

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:35.390
Let me introduce them.

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:36.360
...the Blattaria!

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:37.960
If we materialize them...

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:39.960
...mere flesh and bone.

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.520
Their power is the presence of the nonmaterial within them.

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:44.370
It seems she doesn't like me.

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:46.960
When our strength is needed, please call anytime.

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:51.540
I will respond tolerantly to any womanly changes of heart.

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:53.530
Hayato Kazamatsuri
